    {
      "heading": "The lead–acid battery",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Car batteries use lead, lead four oxide and sulfuric acid.",
          "write": "Pb, PbO₂, H₂SO₄"
        },
        {
          "say": "Each cell gives about two volts. Six in series give 12 volts.",
          "write": "6 × 2 V = 12 V"
        },
        {
          "say": "On discharge, lead is oxidised to lead sulfate.",
          "write": "Pb + SO₄²⁻ → PbSO₄ + 2e⁻"
        },
        {
          "say": "Lead oxide is reduced, also to lead sulfate.",
          "write": "PbO₂ → PbSO₄"
        },
        {
          "say": "Solid lead sulfate forms on both electrodes and stays put.",
          "write": "PbSO₄ on BOTH"
        },
        {
          "say": "Overcharging electrolyses water, making hydrogen and oxygen. That is a hazard.",
          "write": "overcharge → H₂ + O₂"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
